      "message": "I\u0027m hesitant to do this because there may be other components (tests, mostly) that depend on being able to disable `CC_DPTF`. I think we need to think more deeply on how to nicely integrate zephyr and legacy logging before we go making changes throughout the codebase: the status quo is pretty messy and seems like it may have a lot of bugs lurking inside.\n\nI\u0027ve commented this on the bug as well, but:\n\n * The `chan` console command can\u0027t currently control zephyr logs and we know that at least some tests depend on this being able to suppress output other than what they care about.\n * Zephyr logs don\u0027t currently end up visible to the AP (for feedback reports, etc) because nobody turns on `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_LOG_BACKEND_CONSOLE_BUFFER`. This probably needs to be enabled, but can\u0027t be done with minimal logging (which we currently use).",
